* ''Each browser tab asks for its own unlock.'' A tab that attaches to the shared holder opens the keystore by its own ask of the person; the holder carries no unlock between tabs. The reason reads off the session law: a session wears its own face, so each tab answers for its own opening (#/rulings, a session wears the face). The ask admits a tab to its face's open hive and derives no key: the holder keeps a face's keys while some session of that face stands unlocked, and the last to close locks it (operator, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026`>> #/what-both-faces-hold). Item `B1` carries the build. The tab's ask lights its face, and the browser's light lasts while a session stands, where the node's lasts across a vessel's sleep at its pūlama: a host binding the isomorphic rule names, never a split contract.

